def tbl(head,rows,size=8):
 t=d.add_table(rows=1,cols=len(head));t.style='Light Shading Accent 1'
 for c,v in zip(t.rows[0].cells,head):c.text=str(v)
 repeat=OxmlElement('w:tblHeader');t.rows[0]._tr.get_or_add_trPr().append(repeat)
 for row in rows:
  for c,v in zip(t.add_row().cells,row):
   c.text='' if v is None else str(v)
   for pp in c.paragraphs:
    pp.paragraph_format.space_after=Pt(3)
    for run in pp.runs:run.font.size=Pt(size)
 return t
def head(t):d.add_heading(t,1)
head('1. Executive delivery basis and management decisions')
para(f'The recovery scenario contains {D["statistics"]["activities"]} planned activities/milestones ({D["statistics"]["nonzero"]} nonzero tasks). It assumes commencement1November2026, two fabrication lines, one strengthening cell, three strengthening crews, separate installation/support capacity and sequential heavy-lift/cargo reservations. The earliest internal handover milestone is15June2027. These are conditional planning results, not commitments.')
para('The controlling physical interfaces are survey-to-design, checked material release-to-fabrication, jacket/landing readiness-to-installation, BHS service acceptance-to-demolition, and completed inspections/records-to-handover. Appoint a single Project Director and package owners; retain separate technical, client-operational and vessel authority.')
tbl(['Requirement','Preparedcontent','Status','Remaining'],coverage)
head('2. Source hierarchy and document control')
para('Read the executed contract and controlling addenda together. Apply the uploaded BRRP-specific PartII with general structural PartI Rev14. The general structural criteria repeated in Section3 match, but S&SRP/WSSRP-2 project-specific provisions are not silently added to BRRP. Maintain numbered revisions, controlled transmittals, comment resolution, superseded-drawing withdrawal and signed release evidence.')
tbl(['ID','Source','File / location','Application'],[[x[0],x[1],x[2]+'; '+x[3],x[4]] for x in G['sources']])
head('3. Scope of work and bridge boundaries')
para('Common scope: records review, pre-engineering and construction surveys, engineering, procurement, fabrication, inspection/coating, temporary works, loadout, transport, marine support, offshore work, testing/commissioning, demolition where specified, accepted measurements and as-built handover. Confirm interfaces and any company supply explicitly; do not assume platform cranes, accommodation or storage are available.')
tbl(['Bridge','Worktype','StructuralrowMT','DemolitionMT','Handrailm','Gratingm2','GIsheetm2'],[[b[0],b[1],sum(b[2:6]),b[6],b[7],b[8],b[9]] for b in B])
bullets(['Replacement ICW–ICG and ICP–ICG: new lower-deck bridges, fixed-intent/hinged and sliding support interfaces, landing/deck extensions and modifications, applicable jacket strengthening, access fittings and electrical interfaces.','BHS–SLQ: new bridge and supports, landings, piping/cable/lighting/support interfaces, roofing/cladding, lifeboat/muster and safety-study interfaces as specified; install/commission the new facility before removal of the old bridge.','Seven strengthening bridges: verify corrosion and scope, establish approved access/temporary conditions, strengthen specified members/joints/landings, restore grating/handrails/sheeting as applicable, inspect and accept. Do not derive full work quantities only from tonnage.','All modified facilities and temporary arrangements require planned restoration/closure. Scope questions and source-reference conflicts remain in a controlled technical-query register.'])
head('4. Design basis and structural engineering programme')
for x in G['p4criteria']:para(f'{x[0]}: {x[1]} {x[2]}. Source {x[3]}. Status {x[4]}.')
para('Design sequence: validate survey, coordinates and datums; establish actual loads and combinations; reconstruct member connectivity/groups and restraints; reproduce source gravity checks; run strength/stability/serviceability; check joints, fatigue/VIV and movements; transfer concurrent signed reactions to existing platform models; engineer temporary/marine conditions. Independent model reproduction and member/connection/bearing resistance design remain open.')
para('The source braced space-truss models use56/84/42m lengths, compared with approximate reported gaps54.5/80.5/40m. These are not final shop dimensions. Source fixed-support language must not be interpreted as fully moment-rigid restraint. Clarify the BHS SLQ support-wording conflict.')
tbl(['Bridge','Sourcevertical/limitmm','Sourcelateral/limitmm','Listedmember/jointUC'],[[b['name'],f'{b["dv"]}/{b["vlimit"]:.0f}',f'{b["dh"]}/{b["hlimit"]:.0f}',f'{b["uc"]}/{b["juc"]}'] for b in P4['bridges']])
para('These are transcribed source analysis results with independently recalculated criterion limits; no new global analysis is claimed. P4 arithmetic, thermal/section calculations and source-based sheets are carried forward as development evidence, not final design.')
head('5. Detailed engineering and AFC preparation')
bullets(['Maintain a calculation-to-drawing matrix. Each GA, member schedule, connection, bearing and landing detail must cite a checked calculation and survey revision.','For new bridges prepare framing, secondary steel, access, service supports, bearings, end connections, platform strengthening, temporary works, lifting/transport interfaces and detailed MTO. BHS also needs service-transfer and demolition engineering.','For strengthening bridges prepare existing-condition markups, member/joint repairs, temporary load paths, landing interfaces, access/fittings and inspection workpacks.','Engineering checking includes geometry, actual material grade/toughness, effective lengths, local effects, welds/bolts, corrosion basis, fatigue details, movement envelopes, tolerances and inspectability. Do not infer these from screenshots.','AFC workflow: prepare → discipline check → independent/technical review as required → multidisciplinary/interface clearance → ONGC review as applicable → close comments → authorised release/transmittal.','No drawing is stamped AFC, signed or assigned a fictitious approval date in this package. For-review title blocks, registers and review sheets support later release; they are not approved drawings.'])
para(f'The deliverable register contains {len(G["deliverables"])} proposed documents/drawings. P4 source-based development sheets are included in the package as reference material; all applicable open engineering items remain visible.')
head('6. MTO, measurement and material control')
para('The source MTO is indicative and must be developed into member/plate/component quantities from detailed engineering. Separate structural additions, demolition, grating, handrails, sheeting, services and temporary works. Tender steel quantities are not lift weights. Procurement requires material specifications, cut sizes, lengths, grades, certificates and wastage rules.')
tbl(['Category','Calculatedrows','Printedsourcetotal','Difference','Action'],mtocheck)
para('The1MT steel discrepancy comes from existing landing/deck strengthening216MT by rows versus217MT printed. Additional checks establish1166m handrail by rows versus1168m printed and718m2 grating versus719m2 printed. Retain both versions; no silent correction or purchase release.')
para('Addendum jacket wraps are an overlay requiring inclusion reconciliation: ideal shell estimates from P4 are2.479MT ICG,3.092MT ICP and0.346MT BHS. They exclude gaps, quarter fabrication, welding, allowances, corrosion/fit and wastage; do not add them to tender totals or order them without confirming existing inclusion and detailing.')
bullets(['Issue controlled MTO revision and material requisition per bridge/workpack.','Receive with certificates, heat/mark identification and inspection records; segregate nonconforming material.','Track receipt, storage, preservation, issue, installed quantities, surplus and returns.','Record accepted measurement and digital e-MB evidence as required for certification/billing; progress quantities and commercial quantities may use different rules.'])
head('7. Procurement and subcontract management')
para('The25package procurement plan is a preparation register. No enquiry, order or charter has been issued. Vendor lists/agency provisions must be read with amendments; technical suitability, commitments and applicable client review still apply.')
bullets(['Create approved requisitions and bid packages with drawings, specifications, quantities, inspection, documentation, packing and delivery requirements.','Obtain comparable quotations; perform technical and commercial evaluations; verify subcontractor facilities and capacity.','Use authorised purchase commitments only after funding and delegated approval. Flow down applicable contract, HSE, QA, insurance, documentation and change requirements.','Expedite engineering/manufacturing/inspection/dispatch milestones, not only promised delivery dates.','Treat bearings, lifesaving equipment, cables/piping and specialist services as potential lead-time constraints. The schedule25daybulk-material assumption does not validate every package.','Inspect and release by approved ITP/IRT; control substitutions through engineering and applicable client approval.'])
tbl(['ID','Package','Quantitybasis','Release / issue'],[[x[0],x[1],str(x[3])+' '+x[4] if x[3] is not None else 'TBC',x[5]+'; '+x[10]] for x in G['procurement']])
head('8. Fabrication execution and production control')
bullets(['Audit fabrication bays, cranes, material flow, welding manpower, inspection capacity, coating throughput, storage and loadout access before committing capacity.','Release shop workpacks with current authorised drawings, material/cut lists, member/weld marks, WPS, NDT, tolerances, coating and inspection points.','Verify material identity before cutting; retain traceability through splits, assemblies and repairs.','Sequence preparation, fit-up, welding, NDT, repairs, dimensional acceptance and coating. Use qualified personnel and approved procedures; no welding parameters or inspection percentages are invented.','Conduct constructability and suitable trial-fit checks; record measured interface dimensions and changes.','Protect coating and identification through handling/storage. Issue yard release only after required inspection/NCR closure.','Track accepted stage output and actual labour-hours; separate replacement modules from strengthening kits and offshore labour.','First20daykitrelease is a gate within one35dayproductionstream. It is not additional duplicate cell capacity.','Resolve inspection/coating bottlenecks in the six-weeklookahead. Two lines and one cell are capacity assumptions, not demonstrated throughput.'])
head('9. Marine engineering, logistics and offshore readiness')
bullets(['Establish module dimensions, verified weights/COG and lift boundaries before vessel selection. Do not size a crane from aggregate bridge tonnage.','Check crane curves at actual radii, configuration, stability, deck loading, positioning, operating limits, certification and availability.','Prepare loadout, grillage, sea-fastening and transport analyses against actual vessel/route/motion data and source criteria.','Prepare the required3D lift analysis with rigging/skew/dynamic/weight-COG cases, landing arrangements, guides and temporary conditions.','Obtain required marine assurance/MWS reviews under applicable criteria/specification; no lift is released by a management programme alone.','Plan accommodation, supply, cargo, towage, transfers, field moves, waste/backload and emergency readiness. SCC minimum60special-personnel accommodation is a floor, not proof of capacity for simultaneous crews.','Source methodology does not provide platform accommodation/space or company deck-crane use for construction; arrange contractor-supported resources.','Define weather decision authority, operating limits, forecast windows, suspension/cyclone actions and safe departure. Contractor fleet capability and commitments remain unverified.'])
head('10. Installation and execution methodology')
para('The following are management sequences for developing approved workpacks. They do not specify cutting, welding, rigging or demolition instructions. Every operation requires project-specific engineering, permits and readiness release.')
d.add_heading('10.1 ICW–ICG and ICP–ICG new lower-deck bridges',2)
bullets(['Accept survey and engineering; verify geometry/clearances and existing platform capacity.','Complete applicable ICG/ICP jacket strengthening and landing/deck modifications under checked temporary conditions.','Accept fabricated bridge, dimensions, coating and traceability; verify mass/COG and transport configuration.','Complete loadout/transport releases, site access, permits, SIMOPS and operational interfaces.','Execute the approved lift/landing and support-setting procedure; retain engineered temporary stability until permanent connections are accepted.','Complete permanent connections, bearings/guides, walkway/access fittings and electrical interfaces; inspect and restore coatings.','Verify bearing settings and clearances, accepted quantities, functional checks and package handover.'])
d.add_heading('10.2 BHS–SLQ integrated replacement and services',2)
bullets(['Verify all existing services, new routing, operating significance, tie-ins, isolation requirements and safety/lifesaving/muster interfaces.','Complete required jacket/landing readiness and release the new bridge for approved installation.','Install/connect the new bridge and service supports; complete applicable piping, electrical and instrumentation work and approved tests.','Agree and execute authorised service transfers and reinstatement with ONGC; confirm required new-facility operational acceptance.','Only then release existing bridge demolition after confirming redundant services, isolations, temporary stability and engineered removal/backload plan.','Inspect remaining structures, restore affected facilities, document waste/disposal and close punch/dossiers.'])
d.add_heading('10.3 Seven strengthening bridges',2)
bullets(['Verify existing thickness/condition and authorised repair scope; locate live services and restricted areas.','Issue a complete bridge-specific kit/workpack and prepare approved access, protection and temporary conditions.','Execute authorised strengthening/modification without unapproved load-path changes.','Perform required connection/NDT/dimensional acceptance and coating restoration.','Restore access, grating, handrails/sheeting as applicable; remove temporary arrangements only under authorised sequence.','Record accepted quantities and inspection evidence; close package punch and handover.'])
head('11. Quality, HSE and operational control')
para('Use source specifications/IRT to produce approved inspection/test plans, responsibilities, notices and release points. Maintain competent inspection, material traceability, calibrated equipment, nonconformance/concession control and progressive dossiers.')
tbl(['ID','Stage','Verification','Basis','Responsibility','Release'],G['quality'])
bullets(['Implement permit-to-work, SIMOPS, isolation, hotwork, lifting, work-at-height, dropped-object and marine-transfer controls.','Verify competence, medical/training/certification as applicable; plan fatigue, rotations, rescue and medical evacuation with relevant authorities.','Conduct hazard/constructability reviews, toolbox briefings, inspections, drills and corrective-action follow-up.','Project Director coordinates delivery; technical authority, ONGC operations and vessel authorities retain their respective powers.','Maintain a safe-suspension/second-season plan if weather/calendar scenarios require it; the comparator assumes such a plan and does not prove it.'])
head('12. Testing, commissioning and operational acceptance')
para('Prepare discipline-specific test packs with system boundaries, prerequisites, approved test values, calibrated equipment, witnessing, acceptance criteria, reinstatement and records. No generic hydrotest pressure, insulation threshold or torque is selected here.')
tbl(['ID','Discipline','Scope','Verification','Procedurebasis','Owner','Status'],G['commissioning'])
para('Structural acceptance is not a substitute for service commissioning. BHS transfer requires agreed isolations/tie-ins, functional readiness, restoration and operational authorisation. Demolition is a separate gate after the new bridge/services meet their release requirements.')
